/** @page ncurses_ui_widgetsguide UI Widget Toolkit (NcursesUi)

    @tableofcontents

    @ref ncursesuiintro "NcursesUi" builds reusable controls on the binary terminal API.
    Use it when your program needs focus traversal, layout, menus, and event dispatch rather
    than handling every drawing and input operation directly.

    @section ncurses_ui_arch Architecture

    @ref NcursesUi::Widget "Widget" owns children, geometry, focus state, and a dirty flag.
    Add controls with @ref NcursesUi::Widget::addChild() "Widget::addChild()".
    Layout managers are separate objects: @ref NcursesUi::BoxLayout "BoxLayout" distributes
    space among a container's children; @ref NcursesUi::SplitLayout "SplitLayout" divides the
    first two visible children by ratio or fixed size. They are not child widgets.

    @ref NcursesUi::Application "Application" owns the session, root widget, and event loop.
    Set a root layout with @ref NcursesUi::Application::setRootLayout() "Application::setRootLayout()"
    before @ref NcursesUi::Application::setRoot() "Application::setRoot()" so the initial
    geometry is computed with that layout. @ref NcursesUi::EventDispatcher "EventDispatcher"
    routes input; @ref NcursesUi::FocusManager "FocusManager" handles focus traversal.

    @section ncurses_ui_app List and Status Application

    This complete program places an expanding list above a one-row status bar. Arrow keys
    change the selection; \c q exits. The session is closed even if drawing or a callback raises.

    @code{.py}
%modern
%requires ncurses
%requires NcursesUi

Ncurses::Session session();
on_exit session.close();
NcursesUi::Application app(session);
NcursesUi::Widget root();
NcursesUi::ListWidget choices();
choices.setItems(({"label": "Build"}, {"label": "Test"}, {"label": "Deploy"}));
NcursesUi::StatusBarWidget status();
status.setSegments(({"text": "Arrow keys select; q quits"},));
root.addChild(choices);
root.addChild(status);
NcursesUi::BoxLayout layout(NcursesUi::Orientation::Vertical);
app.setRootLayout(layout);
app.setRoot(root);
choices.setFocused(True);
app.setGlobalKeyHandler(hash<NcursesUi::EventResult> sub (hash<Ncurses::InputEvent> event) {
    if (event.type == Ncurses::InputType::Char && event.ch == "q") {
        app.quit();
        return <NcursesUi::EventResult>{"handled": True};
    }
    return <NcursesUi::EventResult>{"handled": False};
});
app.run();
    @endcode

    @ref NcursesUi::StatusBarWidget "StatusBarWidget" already requests a fixed height of one row.
    Other controls can set their sizing preferences with
    @ref NcursesUi::Widget::setVSizePolicy() "Widget::setVSizePolicy()" and
    @ref NcursesUi::Widget::setPreferredSize() "Widget::setPreferredSize()".
    @ref NcursesUi::Application::run() "Application::run()" draws dirty widgets, reads input,
    dispatches events, and invokes registered tick callbacks until
    @ref NcursesUi::Application::quit() "Application::quit()" is called.

    @section ncurses_ui_panels Panel Widgets and Modal Dialogs

    @ref NcursesUi::PanelWidget "PanelWidget" draws in its own
    @ref Qore::Ncurses::Panel "Panel". @ref NcursesUi::DialogWidget "DialogWidget" adds a
    title, message, and buttons. Create it with the application's session, center it, and
    register button/dismiss callbacks before @ref NcursesUi::Application::pushModal() "Application::pushModal()".
    The button callback receives an integer index and string label. Always remove the modal
    with @ref NcursesUi::Application::popModal() "Application::popModal()" when dismissing it.

    This standalone confirmation example exits after either button or Escape:

    @code{.py}
%modern
%requires ncurses
%requires NcursesUi

Ncurses::Session session();
on_exit session.close();
NcursesUi::Application app(session);
NcursesUi::Widget root();
app.setRoot(root);
NcursesUi::DialogWidget dialog(session, "Confirm", "Continue?", ("Yes", "No"));
hash<Ncurses::Size> size = session.screen().size();
dialog.centerOn(size.rows, size.cols);
dialog.setOnButton(sub (int index, string label) {
    app.popModal();
    dialog.hide();
    app.quit();
});
dialog.setOnDismiss(sub () {
    app.popModal();
    dialog.hide();
    app.quit();
});
app.pushModal(dialog);
app.run();
    @endcode

    Child frames remain in screen coordinates inside a panel. For example, an
    input inside a panel at (3, 5) with one-cell border starts at (4, 6).
    Custom widgets draw using @ref NcursesUi::Widget::drawContentRect() "drawContentRect(window)";
    mouse handlers continue to use @ref NcursesUi::Widget::contentRect() "contentRect()".
    Tree drawing clips children to ancestor content bounds. Panels retain child
    offsets when moved; their layout override can recompute sizes after resize.
    On very small screens, dialogs show the focused action and Tab reaches the
    others. Up/Down and PageUp/PageDown scroll wrapped message text; on a one-row dialog they show the message in place
    of the action, and Tab returns to the action labels.

    @section ncurses_ui_tables Sortable and Filterable Tables

    Configure a stable row key before refreshes to preserve selection. Column
    type \c number accepts numbers and numeric strings; \c date requires dates;
    \c string compares displayed text; default \c auto orders nulls, numbers,
    dates, then text. Equal keys retain input order in either direction.
    Comparator/data validation failures leave the old view intact. Selection
    notifications run after committing coherent state and can propagate errors.

    This example sorts service latency numerically, preserves the selected ID,
    and filters displayed values. Arrow keys navigate, Enter/double-click activates,
    and Left/Right reveals fixed-width columns. Press \c q to exit.

    @code{.py}
%modern
%requires ncurses
%requires NcursesUi

Ncurses::Session session();
on_exit session.close();
NcursesUi::Application app(session);
NcursesUi::TableWidget table();
table.setColumns((
    {"key": "name", "header": "Service", "width": 24},
    {"key": "latency", "header": "Latency (ms)", "width": 16, "type": "number", "align": "right"},
));
table.setRowKey("id");
table.setRows((
    {"id": "api", "name": "API", "latency": 10.5},
    {"id": "worker", "name": "Worker", "latency": "2.5"},
));
table.setSortColumn("latency");
@assert(table.getRows()[0].id == "worker");
@assert(table.getSelectedRowData().id == "api");
table.setFilter("api");
@assert(table.getRows().size() == 1);
app.setRoot(table);
app.getFocusManager().setFocus(table);
app.setGlobalKeyHandler(hash<NcursesUi::EventResult> sub (hash<Ncurses::InputEvent> event) {
    if (event.type == Ncurses::InputType::Char && event.ch == "q") {
        app.quit();
        return <NcursesUi::EventResult>{"handled": True};
    }
    return <NcursesUi::EventResult>{"handled": False};
});
app.run();
    @endcode

    @section ncurses_ui_focus_input Nested Input and Modal Focus

    Use the application's focus manager to select a control. Non-focusable
    containers do not block its keys. A modal suspends the previous focus;
    Tab/Shift+Tab cycle within the modal and popping it restores an eligible
    prior control. A text editor displays a caret; other modal controls hide it.
    Explicit global handlers run first, so return unhandled for keys that belong
    to the form. Use @ref NcursesUi::Application::pushPopup() "pushPopup()" only
    when outside clicks should dismiss the popup and reach the underlying UI.

    This deterministic example exercises a nested text form without an event loop:

    @code{.py}
%modern
%requires ncurses
%requires NcursesUi

Ncurses::Session session();
on_exit session.close();
NcursesUi::Application app(session);
NcursesUi::Widget root();
NcursesUi::TextInputWidget command("> ");
root.addChild(command);
app.setRoot(root);
command.setFrameValues(0, 0, 1, 20);
app.getFocusManager().setFocus(command);

NcursesUi::Widget form();
NcursesUi::Widget fields();
NcursesUi::TextInputWidget name("Name: ");
NcursesUi::TextInputWidget region("Region: ");
form.addChild(fields);
fields.addChild(name);
fields.addChild(region);
form.setFrameValues(2, 2, 4, 30);
fields.setFrameValues(2, 2, 4, 30);
name.setFrameValues(2, 2, 1, 30);
region.setFrameValues(3, 2, 1, 30);
app.pushModal(form);
app.processEvent(<Ncurses::InputEvent>{"type": Ncurses::InputType::Char, "ch": "José"});
app.processEvent(<Ncurses::InputEvent>{"type": Ncurses::InputType::Char, "ch": "\t"});
@assert(app.getFocusManager().getCurrentFocus() == region);
@assert(name.getText() == "José");
app.drawAll();
app.popModal();
@assert(app.getFocusManager().getCurrentFocus() == command);
    @endcode

    Input cursor indices remain Qore character offsets. An external index inside
    a combining or emoji cluster snaps to its start. Left/right and deletion
    operate on complete graphemes; @ref NcursesReplUi::InputBuffer::replaceRange()
    "replaceRange()" expands a partial selection before replacing it. Use
    @ref NcursesReplUi::TextPosition "TextPosition" for display-column conversion.

    @section ncurses_ui_widgets_list Standard Widget Components

    |!Widget|!Description
    |@ref NcursesUi::ListWidget "ListWidget"|Selectable scrollable list with keyboard and mouse support
    |@ref NcursesUi::TextInputWidget "TextInputWidget"|Single-line text input with cursor and optional history
    |@ref NcursesUi::ScrollableWidget "ScrollableWidget"|Viewport wrapper with scrollbar rendering
    |@ref NcursesUi::MenuBarWidget "MenuBarWidget"|Horizontal menu bar with dropdown support and Alt+key hotkeys
    |@ref NcursesUi::DropdownMenuWidget "DropdownMenuWidget"|Popup menu for MenuBarWidget items
    |@ref NcursesUi::StatusBarWidget "StatusBarWidget"|Status bar with styled left/right-aligned segments
    |@ref NcursesUi::DialogWidget "DialogWidget"|Modal dialog with message and configurable buttons
    |@ref NcursesUi::FileBrowserWidget "FileBrowserWidget"|Split-pane file system browser
    |@ref NcursesUi::ComboBoxWidget "ComboBoxWidget"|Dropdown selector
    |@ref NcursesUi::CheckboxWidget "CheckboxWidget"|Toggle checkbox
    |@ref NcursesUi::RadioGroupWidget "RadioGroupWidget"|Mutually exclusive radio buttons
    |@ref NcursesUi::TableWidget "TableWidget"|Column-based data table


    @ref NcursesUi::TerminalText "TerminalText" measures display columns, clips at grapheme
    boundaries, and pads Unicode strings for aligned output. See
    @ref ncurses_stylesguide "Style System" for colors and
    @ref ncurses_testingguide "Automated Testing" for deterministic widget tests.

    @section ncurses_ui_editor Multiline Editing and Streaming Output

    TextEditorWidget and TranscriptWidget share source-to-visual mapping with
    ScrollableWidget. Source offsets count Unicode characters at grapheme boundaries;
    screen coordinates count terminal cells. getCaretScreenPosition() returns the
    clipped, scrolled insertion point, or NOTHING when no point is visible. Styled
    prompts participate in wrapping without becoming editable document text.
    Exact-width hard lines reserve an insertion row, keeping their caret distinct
    from the next logical line. Mouse selection, highlights and completion use the
    same geometry as painting.

    Enable bracketed paste on Session; Paste events contain literal payload text.
    TextEditorWidget normalizes CR/LF, expands tabs to four spaces, and drops other
    C0/DEL controls. Enter submits and Alt-Enter adds a newline; setEnterSubmits(False)
    reverses these bindings. Submission and clipboard hooks propagate failures while
    retaining the draft. A submit callback cannot mutate its locked EditorBuffer;
    clear after submit() returns successfully. Ctrl-A selects all in the reusable
    editor; qrepl overrides it with its existing line-home binding.

    This executable model example demonstrates bounded editing, failed-submit
    recovery, searchable transcript blocks and stable selection without a terminal:

    @code{.py}
%modern
%requires ncurses
%requires NcursesUi

NcursesUi::TextEditorWidget editor();
editor.setAutoHeight(1, 6);
editor.setPrompt("request> ");
editor.insertPaste("service status\r\ninclude details");
@assert(editor.getText() == "service status\ninclude details");
editor.getBuffer().undo();
@assert(editor.getText() == "");
editor.getBuffer().redo();
NcursesUi::TranscriptWidget transcript();
transcript.setRetentionLimit(1000);
int request = transcript.appendBlock(("service status", "include details"), "input");
transcript.appendBlock(("API: healthy", "Worker: healthy"), "response");
transcript.setSearch("healthy");
@assert(transcript.getMatches().size() == 2);
transcript.setCollapsed(request, True);
@assert(transcript.getBlockText(request) == "service status\ninclude details");
transcript.setFollowTail(False);
transcript.appendLines(("new event", "another event"));
@assert(transcript.getUnreadCount() == 2);
transcript.returnToLatest();
@assert(transcript.getUnreadCount() == 0);
    @endcode

    TranscriptWidget preserves the reading anchor when following is paused and
    exposes unread count and returnToLatest(). findNext() highlights/navigates literal
    matches; moveBlock() visits submitted-input/response boundaries. setCollapsed()
    hides body rows while retaining identities and source text. select() takes stable
    TextAnchor values; setOnCopy() delivers plain selected text. setLinks() accepts
    validated TranscriptLink ranges and setOnLink() delegates activation to the
    application without opening external resources. Wrapping can be toggled while
    retaining source anchors. Retention removes expired selections and links and
    refreshes search results. Treat getTranscriptContent() as read-only when using
    block metadata; it includes collapse indicators for presentation. getSourceLine()
    and getBlockText() return original plain text. Append, collapse and clear through
    TranscriptWidget. Shift-click retains its original mouse anchor when extending
    across it; scrollbar clicks pause following until the tail is reached.

    LineListContent batches appends, indexes row sums/maximum widths, and retains at
    most two prepared wrap widths. Ordinary appends/edits update affected lines;
    arbitrary insert/remove and width changes rebuild the relevant index/layout.
    Custom providers should return a monotonic getRevision() for automatic repaint.
    Widget::markDirty() invalidates local painting; ancestors inspect descendants.
    Moving/hiding/removing children invalidates exposed parent cells, and overlapping
    later siblings and modal overlays repaint when underlying content changes.
    All models and widget APIs remain confined to the UI thread.

    @section ncursesui_forms Typed Forms and Described Choices

    FormModel stores typed FormField metadata and values, validates required fields,
    choices, custom field predicates and whole-form rules, and publishes named errors.
    Supported types are Text, Multiline, Password, Integer, Number, Boolean and Choice.
    Read-only fields cannot be edited. Invalid numeric drafts remain visible while
    the model retains its last valid typed value. Custom validation for that field and
    whole-form validation wait until parse errors are corrected. Numeric fields reject
    nonfinite values. FormWidget composes wrapped labels,
    help/errors and controls, scrolls focused fields into view, and focuses the first
    invalid field when bound to Application::getFocusManager(). Password controls
    mask whole Unicode graphemes; explicit value/callback APIs still expose the value.

    @code{.py}
%modern
%requires ncurses
%requires NcursesUi
NcursesUi::FormModel form((
    <NcursesUi::FormField>{"name": "name", "label": "Request name", "required": True},
    <NcursesUi::FormField>{"name": "attempts", "label": "Attempts", "type": NcursesUi::FieldType::Integer, "default_value": 3}
));
@assert(!form.validate());
form.setValue("name", "Inspect services");
@assert(form.submit(auto sub (hash<auto> values) { return values.attempts; }));
@assert(form.getResult() == 3);
form.reset();
hash<NcursesUi::FormSubmission> request = form.beginSubmit();
form.cancel();
@assert(!form.complete(request.generation, "stale result"));
    @endcode

    Pending, Running, Cancelled, Failed and Completed states are explicit. During
    validation/submission and after completion, edits and duplicate submits are blocked.
    reset() preserves values; reset(True) restores defaults. Cancellation invalidates
    asynchronous submission generations. Deliver complete()/fail() on the UI thread.
    FormWidget observes programmatic values, schema changes and default restoration.
    Enter submits a single-line field; multiline Enter inserts a newline. Failed submit
    callbacks preserve entered values. TextInputWidget also restores text/cursor on
    submit callback errors, supports atomic single-line paste, and has optional password
    masking and setClearOnSubmit(False) for embedded forms.

    LabelWidget wraps nonfocusable labels. ButtonWidget supplies stable action IDs,
    mouse/keyboard activation, reentrancy protection and optional one-shot completion.
    DescribedChoiceWidget uses ChoiceItem values independently of labels, displaying
    descriptions, recommendations and disabled states. Up/Down/Home/End move the
    highlight, Space chooses, and Enter chooses/submits. Custom responses are typed
    as ChoiceSelection with is_custom=True; invalid or failed submissions retain their
    draft. Successful submission is one-shot until resetSubmission(). See the runnable
    @c examples/forms-inspectors.qr example (F2: inspect, F5: reopen, Ctrl-Q: quit).

    @section ncursesui_inspectors Structured and Code Inspection

    TreeWidget and KeyValueWidget inspect typed hashes, lists and scalar values.
    Nodes have stable JSON Pointer paths; expansion and selection survive replacements
    when paths remain. Filtering includes matches and ancestors without changing saved
    expansion. Traversal is iterative with configurable node/depth bounds. Selection
    changes repaint only the old/new source rows, even for large trees. Control characters
    are escaped in displayed previews. Copy/export callbacks are application-owned and
    never implicitly write a file. Export receives the original typed value and path.

    @code{.py}
%modern
%requires ncurses
%requires NcursesUi
NcursesUi::KeyValueWidget inspector({"service": {"enabled": True, "ports": (8080, 8443)}});
inspector.selectPath("/service/ports/1");
@assert(inspector.getSelectedEntry().value == 8443);
inspector.setFilter("enabled");
@assert(inspector.getVisiblePaths() == ("", "/service", "/service/enabled"));
NcursesUi::CodeViewWidget code("print(1);\r\n", "qore");
code.setHighlighter(string sub (string source, string language) { return "\e[32m" + source + "\e[0m"; });
code.setSearch("print");
@assert(code.getMatches().size() == 1);
@assert(code.getText() == "print(1);\r\n");
    @endcode

    CodeViewWidget provides read-only search, selection, wrapping and syntax styling.
    A highlighter receives normalized display source and a language identifier; it must
    return ANSI-styled text with identical plain content. Styling survives hard newlines.
    Failed/reentrant highlighters preserve the previous document. Selection copies the
    visible normalized text; getText(), copyAll() and exportText() retain exact original
    source, including line endings and tabs. Direct transcript append/retention APIs are
    rejected; replace a document using setText(). The native ANSI parser ignores numeric
    parameters outside the supported integer range without overflow and cooperates with
    cancellation during parsing, measurement, wrapping and drawing.
*/
